urplus just piles up.\n\n| Candidate | Order level (vs forecast) | Estimated cost: good 0 + good 1 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | good 0 at 1.0×, good 1 at 1.05× | ≈ 1,320 + 570 ≈ 1,890 |\n| 2 | about 1.05× and 1.11×, plus a starting buffer of +18/+10 and a smaller final order | ≈ 1,290 + 580 ≈ 1,865 |\n| 6 / 5 | about 1.1× and 1.14× | ≈ 2,240 (5 and 6 are roughly equal) |\n| 1 | about 1.2× and 1.3× | worse still: heavy overbuying and storage, and the day 9 delivery may overflow |\n\n**Why candidate 2 wins.**\n- Its good 0 orders match average demand, since the random multiplier averages about 1.046.\n- The extra stock in its first order protects the early days, when shortages are most likely.\n- The day 26 order is cut to 30 and 12 units, so the leftover stock gets sold. Leftovers are worth nothing at the end, and candidate 0 would end with about 20 unsold units of good 0.\n- It runs short less often than candidate 0 and doesn't carry the costly surplus of candidates 6, 5 and 1."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 355, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5698, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 355}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-19T03:13:08.635Z", "request_id": "req_011CgAs1gidbXQf4b9wrSULK"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01DS8pm4zi9jDavVcBLrKaYC", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgAs1h